<div class="page">
  <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-bottom: 10px;">Ohio Wesleyan Outcomes</h2>
  <h3 style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 20px;">A Follow-up Study of the Class of <span data-field="graduation_year">{{ graduation_year }}</span></h3>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-bottom: 20px;">September, <span data-field="report_date">{{ report_date }}</span></p>

  <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-bottom: 15px;">This summer Career Services conducted its annual survey to study the career journeys of Ohio Wesleyan graduates. Questionnaires were sent out to Ohio Wesleyan University graduates approximately one year after their graduation. Initially, graduates were e-mailed a link to the survey or, if an e-mail address was not available, mailed a paper copy of the survey with a postage-paid return envelope and instructions about the option of filling out the survey on-line. For those who did not respond to this original communication, individuals who were originally e-mailed were sent a follow-up e-mail reminder and then a paper copy of the survey was sent to them. If graduates did not respond to the paper mailing of the survey, they were sent a postcard reminder. These communications yielded a return rate of <span data-field="response_rate">{{ response_rate }}</span> of the Class of <span data-field="graduation_year">{{ graduation_year }}</span>.</p>

  <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-bottom: 20px;">This report covers the following areas for the Class of <span data-field="graduation_year">{{ graduation_year }}</span>:</p>
  <ul style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
    <li><span data-field="report_section_1">{{ report_section_1 }}</span></li>
    <li><span data-field="report_section_2">{{ report_section_2 }}</span></li>
    <li><span data-field="report_section_3">{{ report_section_3 }}</span></li>
  </ul>

  <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-bottom: 15px;">We hope this report will serve as a reference guide for all faculty, staff, students, parents, and alumni interested in career-related statistics for recent Ohio Wesleyan graduates.</p>

  <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-bottom: 15px;">Even though we continue to face economic challenges as a country, Ohio Wesleyan's Class of <span data-field="graduation_year">{{ graduation_year }}</span> graduates are successfully employed in a variety of areas. The percentage of graduates employed upon graduation or during the first two months following graduation increased by approximately <span data-field="employment_increase_percentage">{{ employment_increase_percentage }}</span> from the Class of <span data-field="previous_graduation_year">{{ previous_graduation_year }}</span>. Securing full-time employment in their field of choice, however, was quite similar to last year—79% for the 2002 graduates compared to 76% for the 2001 graduates. It should be noted that the economic challenges in this country are most likely continuing to affect this figure, as in 2000, 88% of graduates employed full-time reported finding work in their field of choice.</p>

  <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-bottom: 20px;">Thirty-two percent of graduates chose to pursue graduate studies, compared with 34% of 2001 graduates. The current status of the Class of <span data-field="graduation_year">{{ graduation_year }}</span> is as follows:</p>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 30px;">
    <div style="width: 45%;">
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-bottom: 5px;">67% are currently employed</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-bottom: 5px;">21% are enrolled in graduate school</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-bottom: 5px;">11% are enrolled in graduate school and employed</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">1% are involved in other endeavors or were not employed at the time of the survey</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 45%;">
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-bottom: 5px;">Comparison summary data for the Classes of <span data-field="graduation_year_2000">{{ graduation_year_2000 }}</span> and <span data-field="graduation_year_2001">{{ graduation_year_2001 }}</span> are included within the report. If you have any questions or desire additional statistics about the Class of <span data-field="graduation_year">{{ graduation_year }}</span>, please contact Career Services at <span data-field="phone_number">{{ phone_number }}</span>. While personally identifiable information is confidential, we are able to sort information by any field listed within the questionnaire. We hope you find the results of this survey interesting and informative.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 80px;">
    <div style="width: 45%; text-align: left;">
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Sincerely,</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 5px;">Carrie A. Lippert</p>
      <p style="font-size: 9pt; margin-top: 0;">Director of Career Services</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 45%; text-align: right;">
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Nancy A. Westfield</p>
      <p style="font-size: 9pt; margin-top: 0;">Asst. Director of Career Services</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

